# Settings of ONE station agent. Copy this file to ~/.config/abf-platform/station-<name>.env, where <name>
# is the agent's name (letters, digits, underscore, dot only) and is the same name you start with
# `systemctl --user enable --now abf-station@<name>`. Then make it readable by you only:
#   chmod 600 ~/.config/abf-platform/station-<name>.env
# Replace every <...> below. The unit deploy/systemd/abf-station@.service.in reads it (EnvironmentFile=).

# The file that holds the agent's token (a path, never the token itself). It must be inside WSL's own
# home folder, mode 600. The token is made with `abf-platform agent-token new <name> --user <user>` and shown once.
ABF_STATION_TOKEN_FILE=<path-of-the-token-file>

# The deployment root: the folder that holds config/env.yaml.
ABF_STATION_DEPLOYMENT=<deployment-folder>

# The plugin folder that holds scripts/on_site.sh.
ABF_STATION_PLUGIN_ROOT=<plugin-folder>

# Optional: the agent finds `ssh` through PATH. systemd does not read ~/.bashrc, so if ssh is not in the
# default PATH, write the whole PATH on one line (every folder, not only the new one), for example:
#   PATH=<folder-with-ssh>:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin

# systemd does not read ~/.bashrc. When you started this agent by hand, everything you had `export`ed in
# ~/.bashrc reached it; the service gets none of it. Go through every export in ~/.bashrc and write each one the agent
# uses as NAME=value in this file (no `export`). What an agent reads from the environment:
#   - PATH (above): must let it find ssh and, for Google Batch, nextflow, gcloud and Java 17 or newer.
#   - JAVA_HOME=<java-folder>                      if you had it exported (Google Batch).
#   - ABF_STATION_GCP_CREDENTIALS=<key-file-path>  the service-account key file of a Google Batch agent (a path, never its contents).
#   - ABF_STATION_UPLOADS=<uploads-folder>         the folder where the platform keeps waiting uploads (Google Batch /upload page);
#                                                  the same folder as ABF_PLATFORM_UPLOADS of the platform.
#   - Other cloud types: ABF_STATION_AWS_CREDENTIALS, ABF_STATION_AZURE_CREDENTIALS, ABF_STATION_KUBECONFIG (each a file path).
# Each agent has its own file like this one, and is enabled once: systemctl --user enable --now abf-station@<name>.
